  "question": {
    "text": "If two charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are separated with distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;and placed in a medium of dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>. What will be the equivalent distance between charges in air for the same electrostatic force?",
